WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.800
Chapter 05 is about how the
existing estate gets there.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:09.293
The workbook's sources described three
separate kits that repeated most of the same

3
00:00:09.293 --> 00:00:14.550
steps, because the destination is the same:
servers in Arc, workstations in Intune,

4
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.944
NTLM restricted after it's measured,
clean service principal names,

5
00:00:18.944 --> 00:00:22.475
hardened SQL Server, and
Conditional Access enforced.

6
00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:24.975
What differs is who holds
the decision record.

7
00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:30.575
The rule all three obey: the control
plane governs, the data plane executes.

8
00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:36.400
The program holds desired state,
observes, classifies drift and reconciles.

9
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:42.000
Entra ID, Intune, Azure Policy and
Active Directory do the runtime work.

10
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.875
An adapter may call a management API;
it never sits inline in a sign-in.

11
00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:49.130
Every path runs four phases in order,

12
00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:52.437
and nothing is restricted
until it has been measured.

13
00:00:52.437 --> 00:00:54.126
Observe is read-only.

14
00:00:54.126 --> 00:00:56.800
Onboard attaches the management planes.

15
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.388
Harden closes the identity gaps,
only after Phase 1 is signed off.

16
00:01:01.388 --> 00:01:03.863
Watch keeps the estate from drifting back.

17
00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:08.639
Budget at least two weeks of assessment,
treat every first run as a dry run,

18
00:01:08.639 --> 00:01:11.665
deploy Conditional Access
report-only first,

19
00:01:11.665 --> 00:01:15.725
and exclude the emergency access
accounts before enforcing.

20
00:01:15.725 --> 00:01:18.287
Domain unjoin is a separate decision.

21
00:01:18.287 --> 00:01:23.562
The manual path suits small estates and
pilots; the operator owns the change record.

22
00:01:23.562 --> 00:01:28.649
The governed path is for larger estates, or
where an authorizing official must sign:

23
00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:32.187
every state-changing step
carries an approval reference.

24
00:01:32.187 --> 00:01:36.388
The retrofit adopts a hand-modernized
estate without re-enrollment.

25
00:01:36.388 --> 00:01:39.144
Its risk is that registering
the current state

26
00:01:39.144 --> 00:01:41.688
as desired blesses
whatever drift is there.

27
00:01:41.688 --> 00:01:44.150
Every governed operation declares a rung.

28
00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:50.000
The federal ceiling is L3, human
approval, and autonomous L4 is refused.

29
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.320
Where Intune Multi Admin Approval covers
a workload, it is the L3 approval.
